# Line-ending policy, made explicit.
#
# Every text blob in this repo is already stored with LF, and the Windows
# checkout materialises CRLF through core.autocrlf=true. The rules below say
# the same thing in a portable way, so a checkout on any OS gets CRLF in the
# working tree and LF in the object store. They deliberately do NOT renormalize
# existing files: because the blobs are already LF, `git add` after this file
# lands produces no diff.
#
# Do not add `*.css`-style rules for files under tools/theme_v3_*.css without
# checking them first — those are inputs of tools/splice_theme.py.
*.py    text eol=crlf
*.js    text eol=crlf
*.css   text eol=crlf
*.html  text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.md    text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png   binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.db    binary
